{"name":"Sawshark","hex":"#aa7766","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sawshark","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the order Pristiophoriformes of sharks with long, blade-like snouts edged with teeth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sawshark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sawshark","blocks":[{"text":"A sawshark or saw shark is a member of a shark order bearing a unique long, saw-like rostrum edged with sharp teeth, which they use to slash and disable their prey. There are ten species within the Pristiophoriformes, the longnose or common sawshark, shortnose sawshark, Japanese sawshark, Bahamas sawshark, Warren's sixgill sawshark, Anna's sixgill sawshark, Kaja's sixgill sawshark, African dwarf sawshark, Lana's sawshark and the tropical sawshark."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Pristiophorus_nudipinnis.jpg/330px-Pristiophorus_nudipinnis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sawshark"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg/500px-Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg/1280px-Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg/500px-Pristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shortnose sawshark","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APristiophorus_nudipinnis_McCoy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Sketchbook_of_fishes_-_25._%28Longnose%29_Saw_shark_-_William_Buelow_Gould%2C_c1832.jpg/500px-Sketchbook_of_fishes_-_25.